Z||000000||JBGehling||11-19-2000||12:28 PM||||Hey,<BR>   Since I can't seem to find a solid Delorean message board anywhere AND I can't find the actual car within 200 miles, I was wondering if anyone here has ever driven (or owned)a delorean? I really like the doors and the car looks pretty good (granted, it's no 88 GT) but how does it drive? Are the seats comfortable? If you've owned one, do they break often? (etc.)<BR>Josh<BR>The only bad thing would be, if I was to get a DeLorean, I'd probably have to sell my 88 GT.||||reg||5
Z||000001||My7Fieros||11-19-2000||02:00 PM||||Im 28 years old and have wanted a DeLorean since I was 13 (since 1985..think hard enough and you'll figure out why lol).<BR>Even though I eat, breath, and sleep Fieros, I still want a DeLorean more than anything..and I will get one...soon!<BR>Anyway, I have had the expierience of driving several DeLoreans. Lets just put it this way, they are by no means a practical car. If you think a Fiero is hard to get in and out of...you aint seen NUTHIN' yet! lol<BR>They feel somewhat awkward at first, but like anything else, you get used to it. As far as quality, that much I cant help you with...I dont know. All I know is..Ive always wanted one, and I plan on buying one within a year!!!<BR>I believe there is a forum member that owns one or used to..I believe its Mike Schaffer, but Im not positive. <BR>Do a search on DeLoreans through AOL search or whatever internet service you use. There is a DeLorean owners association (which publishes DeLorean world magazine), and there is also a place called DeLorean One in Texas I believe that is the "Fiero Factory" of DeLoreans. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||11-19-2000||02:09 PM||||My cousin in Louisville owns one, and he loves it. He also speaks VERY highly of Fieros. There is one for sale here in Myrtle Beach, at the Autohaus, they've got lots of Mercedes Benz's, BMW's, Porsche's...  I think it's an '83. I don't think they want too much for it. ||||reg||1
