Z||000007||Black88GT||11-19-2000||10:04 PM||||I had the "privelege" of driving a Delorean at the beginning of last summer.  It was 100% stock, and very slow, handled rough too.  If it wasn't for "Back to the Future" and the way the doors open, the car would be forgotten by now IMHO.  It was an attention getter though I'll give it that.<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Tigger||11-20-2000||09:06 AM||||I've always thought Deloreans were cool.<P>Here's an interesting site with a bunch of info on Deloreans I found dinkin' around.<P><A HREF="http://www.entermyworld.com/ihome.html" TARGET=_blank>Tamir's Delorean Site</A><P>There has been talk that Delorean might build another car...<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tiggerblue2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Fiero5||11-20-2000||12:21 PM||||The Delorean is an awesome "exotic" car. Stainless steel body, digital dash in a very  cool interior and the great gull wing doors, make it a semi affordable super car.<BR>I had a business friend who had one quite awhile back, and it was a great car and would turn heads. We went to the shopping plaza one day, and the heads turned as we pulled in. Then we lifted up the doors and what a rush, as everyone came over to check it out and ask him questions. He then moved away and I never saw him or the car again :o(<P>I would hate to have to replace something in it though. Being a true exotic car I guess would also be true with the cost and time in parts of others in it's class too.<P>I wonder what the insurance is like now on one of these??||||reg||1
Z||000010||JohnnyK||11-20-2000||01:43 PM||||I don't want to alarm you, but you've never been in a Delorean, seeing as they don't have a digital dash..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Tigger||11-20-2000||01:58 PM||||This is about as digital as it gets...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.entermyworld.com/myd/pics99/oldinter11x1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Black88GT||11-20-2000||04:10 PM||||I hardly consider the DeLorean a "super" or "exotic" car.  With the ROARING 130 hp engine with a stunning 0-60 time of 8.5 seconds, I would think it goes in with the Dodge Caravan ES' not the Ferrari 360 Modena's or Dodge Viper GTS'.  It is very rare though and an attention getter.  I can't imagine trying to find parts though...  <P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Fiero5||11-20-2000||07:25 PM||||I hate to "alarm" you, but yes I was. And yes it hade a digital dash. Not as fancy as you see now, but it was pretty cool back in 1985 when i got to see one for the first time. Maybe a factory option or an aftermarket, but it was digital. Either case, it was a great car. One photo showing one model with an anolog guage doesn't make all models that way, sorry.<P>As for not considering it a super car based on cars of the last 10 years, you have to remember that these came out about some 20 or so years ago. At that time and even now, all the books you find showing exotic or supercars like Ferrari's, Lambo's, Vector's and the like, also show Deloreans.<BR>Remember that Vipers and the like weren't around in the late 70's and early 80's, so even though the Delorean wasn't a stock monster engine blasting automobile, it was and still is considered an exotic supercar.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000014||My7Fieros||11-20-2000||08:19 PM||||Well said, Fiero5. No, they're not fast by any stretch of the imagination. They are one of those cars that you either love or hate...MUCH like Fieros. Im more into the "head turning" than I am about speed and performance. The speed limit is 55 (or 65/75 depending on what state you live in)..who needs a car with a cagillion horsepower that goes  1000 mph anyway? The DeLorean looks great (IMO) and like them or not, they turn heads!||||reg||1
Z||000015||Black88GT||11-20-2000||08:30 PM||||OK I will concede the DeLorean as an "exotic" car, but not a "super car".  Super cars have super performance, handling etc.  <P>I doubt DeLorean will make anything other then license plates (in Folsom county).  Last I heard he was bankrupt...<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
